================================================================================
ABSTRACT
================================================================================

This repository defines two complementary deterministic simulation paradigms:

  (1) META KERNEL (Research / Formalism Layer)
  (2) REAL ENGINE (Production ECS + Netcode Core)

They represent two interpretations of the same underlying system:

  - META KERNEL: causal lattice, proof geometry, symbolic determinism
  - REAL ENGINE: executable state machine, rollback netcode, ECS runtime

Both systems converge on one invariant:

  STATE(t) = Ξ(INPUT(t), STATE(t-1))
  TRUTH    = S_ECHO(STATE)

================================================================================
PART I — META KERNEL (THEORETICAL LAYER)
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. CORE IDEA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Meta Kernel treats computation as a:

  "causal collapse lattice over discrete entropy inputs"

Each tick is a projection:

  Ξ : (S_{t-1}, I_t) → S_t

Where:
  S = system state manifold
  I = input entropy field
  Ξ = deterministic collapse operator

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. LAYER MODEL (META KERNEL)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Layer 0 — Input Entropy Field
  raw commands / events / adversarial noise

Layer 1 — CDI (Causal Depth Index)
  enforces strict temporal ordering:
  t_cmd ≤ t_system

Layer 2 — Noise Classifier (Ξ_NOISE)
  partitions inputs into:
    VALID / NORMALIZABLE / INVALID

Layer 3 — Collapse Operator (Ξ_COLLAPSE)
  deterministic state transition

Layer 3.5 — Shard Thermodynamics
  measures computational density gradients:
  ∇ entropy(x,t)

Layer 4 — S_ECHO
  global hash projection:

    S_ECHO = H(Σ state components)

Layer 5 — ZK-SYNC
  cryptographic compression of state transition validity

Layer 6 — Consensus Gate
  distributed agreement filter

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. MATHEMATICAL FORMALISM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

State evolution:

  S_t = Ξ(S_{t-1}, I_t)

Hash projection:

  H(S) = ∑ᵢ fold(σᵢ ⊕ pᵢ ⊗ vᵢ)

Entropy bound:

  E(S_t) ≤ E(S_{t-1}) + log(|I_t|)

Collapse stability:

  lim(t→∞) Var(S_t) → 0 under deterministic constraint

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. STRENGTHS (META KERNEL)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- rigorous determinism model
- adversarial reasoning built-in
- ZK-compatible structure
- formal causal interpretation
- theoretical auditability

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. WEAKNESSES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- not directly executable
- high abstraction overhead
- no concrete memory layout
- no transport model
- lacks runtime optimization constraints

================================================================================
PART II — REAL ENGINE (PRODUCTION LAYER)
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. CORE IDEA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Real Engine is a deterministic ECS + lockstep netcode system:

  "simulation = ordered state mutation over fixed-point ECS"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. CORE LOOP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Each tick:

  1. receive commands
  2. validate causality
  3. apply deterministic ECS mutation
  4. integrate physics
  5. compute S_ECHO hash
  6. emit snapshot

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. ECS MODEL (SCALED FOR DETERMINISM)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sparse Set replacement:

  entities: Vec<Entity>
  pos: Vec<Position>
  vel: Vec<Velocity>
  index: Vec<usize>

Guarantee:

  O(1) insert/remove
  deterministic iteration order

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ROLLBACK SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Client maintains:

  SnapshotRingBuffer {
    state[t-N ... t]
  }

On mismatch:

  if client_hash != server_hash:
      rollback_to(last_valid_snapshot)
      replay_inputs()

This is equivalent to:

  S_t = f(S_{t-1}, I_t)
  if divergence:
      recompute forward chain

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. NETWORK MODEL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Transport:

  UDP or QUIC (recommended QUIC for congestion control)

Frame:

  [tick | entity_delta | command_batch | hash]

Delta compression:

  only send changed components per tick

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. HASH FINALITY (S_ECHO)

  H_t = F(S_t)

where F is deterministic fold:

  F = stable iteration hash (FNV-1a variant or custom mix)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. GOLD MASTER STATE (S0)

Initialization:

  S_0 = canonical empty deterministic ECS

All clients MUST derive state from:

  bootstrap(S_0)

No divergence allowed before tick 0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. STRENGTHS (REAL ENGINE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- fully implementable
- production-ready netcode structure
- rollback compatible
- bandwidth efficient (delta compression)
- deterministic cross-platform execution
- compatible with multiplayer lockstep systems

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. WEAKNESSES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- requires strict discipline in floating-point removal
- state divergence debugging is non-trivial
- network desync handling is expensive in worst case
- complexity in snapshot buffer management

================================================================================
PART III — CONCEPTUAL LINKAGE (THEORY ↔ ENGINE)
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. TELEPHONE GAME MODEL (INFORMATION DRIFT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

META KERNEL interpretation:

  I₀ → I₁ → I₂ → ... → Iₙ
  where entropy accumulates unless constrained

REAL ENGINE interpretation:

  server enforces:
    S_t = deterministic recomputation
    prevents drift entirely

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. AZTEC COLOR THEORY ANALOGY (STATE COMPRESSION)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Color perception model:

  observer reconstructs signal from limited channels

Mapping:

  ECS state = full spectrum
  S_ECHO = compressed perceptual projection

Lossless only if:

  hash(S_t) = stable invariant

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. RECURSION / BACKREACTION MODEL

Recursive collapse:

  S_{t+1} = Ξ(S_t, I_t)

Backreaction:

  I_t influenced by previous S_t

This creates a closed loop:

  input ↔ state feedback system

Used for:
  - prediction correction
  - rollback stabilization
  - adversarial resistance

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. SONOLUMINESCENCE ANALOGY (COMPRESSION EVENT MODEL)

Physical analogy:

  energy → bubble collapse → photon burst

Mapping:

  entropy input → Ξ_COLLAPSE → S_ECHO emission

Interpretation:

  computation behaves like energy compression event:
  unstable inputs collapse into stable observable state

================================================================================
PART IV — SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE DECISION
================================================================================

The repository is split into:

/core
  deterministic ECS + tick engine + S_ECHO

/net
  transport layer + delta compression

/client
  prediction + rollback buffer

/test
  deterministic validation suite

================================================================================
FINAL INVARIANT
================================================================================

There exists only one truth carrier:

  S_ECHO(state_t)

Everything else is either:

  - prediction
  - compression
  - or discarded entropy

